🔥 Project Goal

Build a modular AWS infrastructure using Terraform for a Kubernetes-based platform

👉 In your project, Terraform creates:

Network layer using VPC
Ingress layer using NLB
DNS layer using Route53
Container platform using EKS

👉 This is a practical DevOps architecture because it separates networking, load balancing, DNS, and compute into reusable modules

🔥 Project Architecture

High-level flow:

Users -> Route53 DNS -> Network Load Balancer -> EKS workloads

Underlying infrastructure:

Custom VPC
3 public subnets
3 private subnets
Internet Gateway for public internet access
NAT Gateway for outbound internet from private subnets
EKS cluster across subnets
Managed node group in private subnets
Route53 record pointing to the NLB

